   "change": "17 ext075 baseline LPs replaced by the V32 A-stage baselines of the identical electrical LP (cut 0.3, ext 0.75)",
   "reason": "CPU contention (about 6 min per LP) and earlyoom terminations; V32 B0 asserted that the gas-profile split does not change the electrical baseline optimum",
   "results_read_before_change": "none for ext075"
  },
  {
   "id": "amendment_02",
   "registered_utc": "2026-11-02T07:44:29.938193Z",
   "change": "greedy.py: when stock is below the protective floor, the boost now reserves the compression fuel needed to refill to the floor (1 + kappa/eta per MWh stored). main_greedy_rule_eens_WS21 failed on the old rule with an inventory-floor exception and is re-run; WS13 was terminated three times by earlyoom without a receipt and is re-run.",
   "effect_on_completed_runs": "none: runs without an exception never entered the corrected branch (otherwise the floor check would have raised); profiles for WS03 and WS05 recomputed identically",
   "failed_receipts_retained": [
    "results/main_greedy_rule_eens_WS21.attempt_failed_*.json",
    "results/main_greedy_rule_eens_WS13.attempt_failed_*.json"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "amendment_03",
   "registered_utc": "2026-11-02T08:03:16.276221Z",
   "change": "execution order only: cut05ext075 baselines (calibration) moved before ext075, uk and cut05ext075 evaluations; no case definitions changed",
   "reason": "calibration of the new boundary is needed early given about 6 to 8 min per LP under CPU contention"
  },
  {
   "id": "amendment_04",
   "registered_utc": "2026-11-02T11:45:00.523866Z",
   "change": "server reboot at about 10:43 UTC stopped the queue; three cases that had been terminated three times by earlyoom before the reboot (cut05ext075_baseline_WS19, ext075_eval_rule_eens_WS06, ext075_eval_rule_resource_WS06) are re-run; their failure receipts are retained as *.attempt_failed_*.json",
   "reason": "no scientific failure; processes were killed for memory without writing a receipt"
  },
  {
